<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hausbergen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1262</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hausbergen was fought on 8 March 1262 near Strasbourg between the city's citizen militia and the army of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-of-geroldseck">Walter of Geroldseck</a>. The townsmen won a decisive victory, ending the bishop's lordship over the city. Strasbourg became in effect a free imperial city governing itself, while the bishops moved their seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saverne">Saverne</a> and ruled only their lands outside it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hausbergen.jpg" alt="Battle of Hausbergen" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Émile Schweitzer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bataille_de_Hausbergen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
